# dbt

## Naming (from engineering_standards.md §1)

- Staging: `stg_<source>__<entity>`
- Base: `base_<domain>__<entity>`
- Core: `dim_<entity>`, `fct_<entity>`
- Intermediate: `int_<domain>__<purpose>`
- Marts: `mart_<domain>__<purpose>`
- Columns: snake_case; booleans `is_`/`has_`; timestamps `_at`; dates `_date`

## Where rules live (do not re-derive here)

- Layer contract: [`docs/layering.md`](../../docs/layering.md)
- Testing, SQL structure, CI gate: [`docs/engineering_standards.md`](../../docs/engineering_standards.md)
- Stock-specific: [`docs/project_context.md`](../../docs/project_context.md)

## Mandatory guardrails

- `1_staging`: one `stg_*` model per raw source table; no cross-source joins.
- Staging SQL under `models/1_staging/<source>/`, never at `1_staging/` root.
- `4_intermediate` must not `ref('mart_*')`.
- Every model and every `dbt_analytics/tests/*.sql` file starts with `WITH` + import CTE per `ref()`; named CTE chains only (§1.1).
- No scalar subqueries in `SELECT`; no `FROM (SELECT ...)`.
- Do not cite "dbt standard" to skip [`engineering_standards.md`](../../docs/engineering_standards.md) §1.1 — repo rules win.
- Every new model needs at least one meaningful test.

## Documentation (same PR as model changes)

- Every model and **every column** needs a YAML `description` (see engineering_standards §2).
- Model description anatomy: `**What:**`, `**Grain:**`, `**Source:**` (staging may use Source instead of What), `**Used by:**` for core+.
- Column descriptions: business meaning, unit/scale, when null.
- Card metrics and eligibility: align with [`docs/data_contract.md`](../../docs/data_contract.md); use `dbt_analytics/models/_docs.md` doc blocks for long shared text.
- Add `meta`: `owner`, `domain`, `criticality` on every model.

Before opening a PR:

```powershell
python scripts/check_dbt_sql_structure.py
sqlfluff lint dbt_analytics/models dbt_analytics/tests
$env:DBT_RAW_PATH="storage/raw"
dbt build --project-dir dbt_analytics --profiles-dir .
dbt docs generate --project-dir dbt_analytics --profiles-dir .
python scripts/check_dbt_documentation.py
```

CI fails if descriptions are missing or grain-only one-liners.

## Tooling

- Sync registry → dbt vars: `python scripts/sync_dbt_vars.py`
- Layer contract: `python scripts/check_layer_contract.py`
- SQL structure: `python scripts/check_dbt_sql_structure.py` + `sqlfluff lint` (see [`.sqlfluff`](../../.sqlfluff))
- Documentation gate: `python scripts/check_dbt_documentation.py`
